          "lore_md": "Fictional-registry attribution doubt: older sources name Omba as Sutekh's first childe; newer doctrine prefers not to count. Either way, the story survives because it is useful: Omba was sent to corrupt a king and instead corrupted the concept of kingship, teaching mortals that law is just fear wearing a crown. The clan's Corrupters still study the Omba method — never attack a virtue, price it. His last confirmed appearance was a marketplace in 1911 where three missionaries renounced their vows in an afternoon. The Society of Leopold keeps a file on him thicker than on most methuselahs, which, given that he may not exist, is either a compliment or a trap he set in 3000 BC.",
