          "lore_md": "Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent). The canal is the hinge of the world's trade, and Khalid is the hinge of the canal. Every ship that passes pays someone; the Ministry's cut is indexed in secrets — crew manifests, cargo holds that never open, insurance claims filed by frightened owners. His temple is the water itself: baptisms at the buoy line, sermons to drowned sailors, and a fleet of tug pilots who have served the church for three human generations. The Second Inquisition has audited the canal zone twice and found only logistics companies. Khalid sent them a thank-you fruit basket. The Camarilla's harbormasters call him a partner. His god calls him a tithing house.",
          "photo": "assets/img/char_mini05.png"
