          "lore_md": "Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent). Once a year Alexandria throws a festival, and once a year the festival is Rania's cathedral. She learned the old lesson of the corn — that a city will trade anything for a good season — and built a congregation that renews itself like a tide. Merchants tithe for luck, officials tithe for silence, and the young come for the music and stay for the dreams. Her sermons last exactly one night a year; her administration runs the other 364. The Faithful criticize her carnival style; the Seneschals fund it, because a temple that pays for itself is the church's future. SchreckNET flags the festival nights: three每年 disappearances, none investigated, all waterlogged.",
          "photo": "assets/img/char_mini08.png"
