      "weakness": "Every Tremere is blood bound into the clan's hierarchy — the first drink comes from the regent's cup, and the bond climbs tier by tier to the top of the pyramid.",
      "lore_md": "Before they were Kindred, they were the Order of Hermes: mortal wizards who traded humanity for eternity in 1022 CE, when the magus Tremere and his inner circle — Etrius, Goratrix, Meerlinda — drank cursed vitae and shed death. The price was the Beast, and a thirst no rite has ever quenched. In 1133 the founder committed the founding crime of the modern Jyhad: he hunted down Saulot, the Antediluvian father of the Salubri, and devoured him in his sleep. Every Tremere since has inherited the stolen crown.\n\nThe clan is a pyramid bound in blood. Every childe drinks from the regent's cup and the bond climbs to the top of the tower — a chain of loyalty no other clan would tolerate. From that discipline came the clan's wars: the purge of the Salubri, painted as infernalists to hide a theft; the creation of the Gargoyles, flesh stitched from captured Kindred; and the schism that birthed House Goratrix, the antitribu who kept the old rites without the old oaths.\n\nVienna held the clan's heart for eight centuries — the Chantry, the Council of Seven, the sleeping founder. In 2008 the Second Inquisition burned it to the ground and blamed a terrorist cell. The hierarchy survives as fragments: rebel chantries, wandering sorcerers, archives smuggled out in pieces. On SchreckNET the Tremere are the most hunted signatures on the board — a warlock's aura burns bright in any magical survey, and the Inquisition shoots first. What remains is a clan of survivors: still the deadliest blood-sorcerers walking, still convinced the theft of Saulot was worth it.",
