      "weakness": "Rarefied taste: each Ventrue can feed safely from only a narrow class of mortals and retches from all others.",
      "lore_md": "The Ventrue call themselves the clan of kings, and for once the propaganda is close to true. From the merchant princes of Carthage to the boards of the Fortune 500, the Blue Bloods have operated on one principle: whoever owns the food supply owns the species. Their founder, Veddhartha, taught them that blood is a ledger and Gehenna a balance sheet; his childer have been settling accounts ever since.\n\nThey built the Camarilla with the Tremere in 1450 and have been its spine ever since — every justicar, every prince, every tidy little masquerade is a Ventrue investment paying dividends. Then the Second Inquisition took Vienna, took London, and took Hardestadt himself. For the first time in five centuries the board of directors is missing directors, and the proxies are circling.\n\nSchreckNET watches them more closely than any other clan, because the Ventrue are the most legible of the Damned. They leave paper trails. Board seats, shell companies, campaign donations — every entry in this registry is a window into the feeding hierarchy of the oldest ruling caste. Note the pattern repeated across all twenty dossiers: a Ventrue never holds territory, only leverage. Find the leverage, find the Blue Blood.",
