      "lore_md": "Made, not Embraced: the Gargoyles were manufactured by the Tremere from Gangrel, Nosferatu and Stone-molded vitae in the early thirteenth century, and for seven hundred years they were property. Guardians, sentries, flying muscle — a bloodline with a bill of sale. The revolt of the gargoyles in 1480 (the so-called Virstania flight) took a third of them off the leashes, and their descendants are still out there, nesting in places with only one approach.\n\nTo the rest of the Kindred they are furniture with fangs. To the Second Inquisition they are, briefly, a radar mystery: creatures with no public face, no paper trail, no social media, moving on the wind between spires and smokestacks. To SchreckNET they are the canary: gargoyles roost where the Tremere used to, and the Tremere used to roost where the information is.\n\nAnalysts flag GARGOYLE-NEST whenever a thermal anomaly appears on a structure older than the city below it. Standard advice: gargoyles do not attack first. They report first.\n\nThe bloodline’s tragedy is simple: they remember being made. Ask one about its maker and note the date it stopped answering.",
