          "lore_md": "Two gargoyles, one bloodline entry, because they have not been more than twelve meters apart since they were poured from the same mold in 1402. They fly mirrored routes, answer questions in halves, and have only ever been photographed together in single frames — separately, cameras catch one and a smear. They trade approach-coverage of the port to anyone who respects one condition: no maker’s name spoken aloud on the water. The one analyst who broke the rule reports nothing wrong, except that his microphone now records him before he speaks.",
